The legal texts come from the Palau Code Commission and its Publication And Law Access Unit ("PALAU Office"),
which compile and publish the laws of the Republic of Palau (1 PNC § 1002):

  Constitution of the Republic of Palau (current as of 05/13/2026) and the Palau National Code Annotated (current
  titles as of 09/30/2026; First Edition 1994; 15th-18th Supplements), PDFs on the Code Commission's public Google
  Drive, https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1o9b7uIAaNl7qj_yfILpbgstBp6nW90Ox, linked from
  https://palaulaw.gov.pw/ (retrieved 2026-10-29).

The publisher's notices:

  "Copyright (c) Republic of Palau, Publication And Law Access Unit" (PNC front matter).

  "The Palau Legal Information Access website is a project of the Republic of Palau Code Commission, established to
  provide free, open, and reliable access to the laws of the Republic of Palau." ... "While every effort is made to
  ensure accuracy, the documents provided on this platform are for informational purposes only and do not
  constitute official legal advice." (palaulaw.gov.pw, About)

No licence to republish is given. This repository is therefore private; whether and how it may be published is the
owner's decision.

Changes made by Lexifina: each edition was converted from its PDF text layer to one Markdown file per section,
article or amendment, one paragraph per line; spacing, quotes and dashes were normalised; running heads, page feet,
annotations, tables of contents and Division, Chapter and Subchapter headings were left out; and the versions were
arranged as git commits credited to the laws the Code Commission's notes name for each change. The wording of the
law was not changed. The Palau Code Commission does not endorse this repository.

Lexifina's own contributions (the arrangement of the history, the commit messages, the tables and the tools) are
dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal:
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
